.TH MDT.RENAME_STATS 4 2026-10-06 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.rename_stats \- parent directory sizes of renames on an MDT
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param mdt." FSNAME *.rename_stats
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME *.rename_stats=clear
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 | -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per-MDT device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present for MDT devices.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B rename_stats
parameter reports, for each successful rename handled by this MDT, a
log2-bucketed histogram of the size of the parent directories involved.
Writing any value to the parameter clears it.
.PP
Output is YAML. After the
.BR snapshot_time ", " start_time " and " elapsed_time
of the sampling interval come up to three histograms:
.B same_dir
for renames within one directory,
and
.BR crossdir_src " and " crossdir_tgt
for the source and target parents of renames between two directories.
A histogram with no samples is omitted. Each entry reports the bucket
upper bound in bytes, KB or MB, the number of renames in that bucket
.RB ( sample ),
that bucket's percentage of the total
.RB ( pct ),
and the cumulative percentage
.RB ( cum_pct ).
.PP
The
.B md_stats
parameter of the MDT counts renames with their latency:
.B rename
counts every successful rename,
.BR samedir_rename " and " crossdir_rename
split them as above,
.BR parallel_rename_file " and " parallel_rename_dir
count those that ran without the filesystem-wide rename lock,
.B parallel_rename_remote
those of them whose source parent or source file is on another MDT, and
.B rename_trylocks
those that took it without waiting.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following module:
.EX
.B mdt.*.rename_stats
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show and then clear the rename statistics of the
.B testfs
filesystem's first MDT:
.EX
.RB "mds# " "lctl get_param mdt.testfs-MDT0000.rename_stats"
.RB "mds# " "lctl set_param mdt.testfs-MDT0000.rename_stats=clear"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B rename_stats
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.2.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_1_53_0-35-g7c8ebf7b98
